(a) License required. With the exception of home-brew beverages, it shall be unlawful for any person to manufacture, serve, furnish, sell or offer for sale, at retail or wholesale, within the corporate limits of the city any alcoholic beverage, including malt beverage or wine, without having a manufacturer's license or retail or wholesale alcoholic beverage dealer's license. With the exception of home-brew beverages, it shall be unlawful for any person to manufacture, serve, furnish, sell or offer for sale, at retail or wholesale, within the corporate limits of the city any alcoholic beverage, including malt beverage or wine, in violation of the terms of such license or this chapter.
(b) Classes. The licenses shall be divided into the following classes:
(1) Class A—Retail beer and wine;
(2) Class B—Retail liquor;
(3) Class C—Retail beer and wine by the drink;
(4) Class D—Retail liquor by the drink;
(5) Class E—Wholesale beer and wine;
(6) Class F—Wholesale liquor;
(7) Class G—Alcoholic beverage caterer;
(8) Class H—Brewery;
(9) Class I—Brewpub;
(10) Class J—Hotel;
(11) Class K—Distillery;
(12) Class L—Bottlehouse;
(13) Class M—Specialty gift shop;
(14) Class N—Ancillary winetasting;
(15) Class O—Farm winery.
(Ord. No. 2026-14, § 1(Exh. A), 7-7-26)
